# ApplicationTracker

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 5 — Application System

## Purpose

The single tracking record for every application GrantAI has ever drafted
or the founder has pursued — the file every other component reads from or
writes to when an opportunity moves from "opportunity" to "application in
progress." This is what `ExecutiveGrantAdvisor-Agent` reads to build its
priority view, and what `GrantHunter-Agent` checks before starting a new
draft (to avoid duplicating an existing one).

## Record Schema

```
- Opportunity name: (matches the entry in FederalGrants.md / etc.)
- Business: (which BusinessProfiles.md entry this is for)
- Status: draft → review-passed / review-failed → founder-review →
  submitted → awarded / declined / withdrawn
- Fit score: (from ScoringSystem.md at time of drafting)
- Deadline:
- Drafted by: (GrantWriter-Agent, on-demand or Hunter-triggered)
- Reviewed by: (GrantReviewer-Agent — pass/fail notes)
- Compliance notes: (from GrantCompliance-Agent)
- Founder decision: (pending / approved to submit / declined / revise)
- Submitted date: (blank until founder actually submits — Tier 4 action,
  never set by any agent)
- Outcome: (blank until known)
- Last updated:
```

## Status Flow

```
draft → review-passed/review-failed → founder-review
     → [founder submits externally, then marks: submitted]
     → awarded / declined / withdrawn
```

Note the gap between `founder-review` and `submitted` — no agent moves an
entry into `submitted` status. Only the founder does, after actually
submitting the application through the funder's own process. This tracker
records reality; it doesn't cause it.

## Feeds

- `ExecutiveGrantAdvisor-Agent` — priority view of what needs attention
- `ContinuousLearning.md` (Phase 7) — outcome data (awarded/declined) feeds
  back into scoring calibration
- `Metrics.md` (Phase 7) — aggregate stats (applications drafted, win rate,
  total funding pursued/awarded)

